          "name": "Defensive",
          "pokemon": "Arceus-Electric",
          "shiny": false,
          "gender": "DC",
          "levels": [],
          "description": "<p>Arceus-Electric's main draw is its Electric typing, which grants it both STAB on Thunder Cage and a resistance to it, giving Arceus-Electric a niche over other mostly neutral options like <a href=\"/dex/sv/pokemon/arceus/bh/\" hreflang=\"en\">Arceus</a>. Ice Beam provides generally good coverage, hitting Dragon- and Ground-types like <a href=\"/dex/sv/pokemon/eternatus/bh/\" hreflang=\"en\">Eternatus</a> and <a href=\"/dex/sv/pokemon/garchomp-mega/bh/\" hreflang=\"en\">Mega Garchomp</a> that can otherwise switch into Thunder Cage safely. Secret Sword is an option that lets Arceus-Electric bypass <a href=\"/dex/sv/pokemon/blissey/bh/\" hreflang=\"en\">Blissey</a>, an otherwise hard stop to it that also denies Strength Sap healing. Ice Scales variants can struggle to answer powerful threats like <a href=\"/dex/sv/pokemon/alakazam-mega/bh/\" hreflang=\"en\">Mega Alakazam</a> and <a href=\"/dex/sv/pokemon/flutter-mane/bh/\" hreflang=\"en\">Flutter Mane</a> long-term, making a secondary specially defensive teammate, such as a RegenVest user or Blissey, helpful. Fur Coat variants can handle most physical threats but are notably weak to Mega Garchomp, making a teammate like <a href=\"/dex/sv/pokemon/celesteela/bh/\" hreflang=\"en\">Celesteela</a> or a secondary Fur Coat user necessary. Arceus-Electric usually can Imposter-proof itself, but Pokemon like Imposter <a href=\"/dex/sv/pokemon/chansey/bh/\" hreflang=\"en\">Chansey</a> can act as a secondary Imposter-proofer if it is weakened or inflicted with Salt Cure.</p>",
